 "name": "PSM712-LF-T7",
 "kind": "tvs",
 "manufacturer": "ProTek Devices",
 "title": "PSM712: 600 W asymmetrical two-line TVS array for RS-485, SOT-23",
 "source": {
  "document": "05094",
  "revision": "R13, 10/25",
  "pages": 7
 },
 "summary": "A two-channel transient voltage suppressor in SOT-23 that guards a pair of data lines against ESD, fast transients and surge. Each line, pin 1 and pin 2, meets the common pin 3 through two avalanche diodes in series with opposed polarity, so it clamps in both directions but at different levels: it stands off 12 V with the line positive and 7 V with pin 3 positive. It is aimed at RS-485 transceivers. Each line takes 600 W peak for an 8/20 µs pulse. PSM712-LF-T7 is the lead-free part on a 7-inch reel of 3000.",
