 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Structure",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Two independent channels share pin 3. Between each I/O pin and pin 3 sit two avalanche diodes in series, anode to anode: a 12 V one conducting in avalanche when the I/O pin goes positive, and a 7 V one when it goes negative. Each line conducts in both polarities, at different voltages."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Intended use",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Applications: RS-485 transceivers, network interfaces, wireless systems and portable electronics. Threats covered: ESD, tertiary lightning, switching transients. Standards met: IEC 61000-4-2, 61000-4-4 and 61000-4-5; the surge rating is Level 2 line to ground and Level 3 line to line."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Pulse rating",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "The 600 W rating is for the 8/20 µs pulse: 8 µs rise to peak, falling to half the peak current at 20 µs. Peak pulse power falls as pulse duration grows, from about 7.8 kW at 0.1 µs to about 30 W at 10 ms. Above 25 °C ambient the peak pulse power derates linearly to 40 % at 150 °C, and the average power to zero at 150 °C."
  }
 ],
